{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB11800 - MONDO_5549",
  "verbalization": "Tivozanib, a multitargeted kinase inhibitor, is implicated in the treatment of renal cell carcinomas through a complex pathway involving Everolimus. The evidence suggests that Tivozanib is associated with Renal Cell Carcinoma (disease) and Everolimus, which in turn is linked to Renal Cell Adenocarcinoma. This indicates a potential mechanism where Tivozanib may influence the progression or treatment of renal cell carcinoma by modulating the Everolimus signaling pathway. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Tivozanib to Renal Cell Adenocarcinoma highlights the possibility of a broader therapeutic role, possibly through indirect mechanisms involving the Everolimus pathway. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering the interplay between Tivozanib and Everolimus in the context of renal cell carcinoma treatment.",
